======================================================================
1. EVIDENCE-STATUS DEFINITIONS
======================================================================

Each result or numerical artifact must be assigned one of the following
evidence states.

STATUS A — SPECIFIED

The quantity or computational output was defined as part of the study
design or model specification.

STATUS B — DOCUMENTED / REPORTED

The quantity is present in a recovered figure, table, workbook,
manuscript draft, note, or other downstream representation, but the
underlying machine-readable or native computational execution artifact
has not yet been recovered.

STATUS C — EXECUTED — EVIDENCE RECOVERED

The corresponding COMSOL solution, numerical export, solver output,
batch execution record, or equivalent computational artifact has been
recovered.

STATUS D — VERIFIED

The underlying execution artifact has been recovered and the result has
passed the applicable predefined verification checks.

STATUS E — MANUSCRIPT-REPORTED

The result has complete traceability through patient input,
computational execution, verification, and result extraction and is
therefore suitable for use as a definitive quantitative manuscript
result.

IMPORTANT CONTROL RULE:

STATUS B must not automatically be upgraded to STATUS C.

STATUS C must not automatically be upgraded to STATUS D.

STATUS D must not automatically be upgraded to STATUS E.

A downstream figure or table does not independently establish the
existence of a native COMSOL solution file.

