19. PROHIBITED RESULT-RECONSTRUCTION PRACTICES
======================================================================

The following practices are prohibited:

1. Back-calculating patient-level values from group means.

2. Inventing missing COMSOL numerical outputs.

3. Altering values solely to make figures and tables agree.

4. Treating graphical appearance as proof of numerical execution.

5. Treating a planned simulation as an executed simulation.

6. Treating a documented result as a verified result without supporting
   evidence.

7. Creating artificial historical solver logs and representing them as
   original execution records.

8. Inferring missing cavity-pressure or basal-constraint parameters from
   desired numerical results.

9. Calling recovered reference comparisons independent validation without
   establishing the calibration/model-lock/validation provenance.

10. Reporting myocardial-volume results where no traceable myocardial-
    volume dataset is currently available.

